  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta =2,$ where $\\theta =m\u2220A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{\u2015}{AC}$ adjacent to $\u2220A.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{BC}{15} \\\\ BC & =2\\cdot 15 \\\\ BC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =225.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
